On Thursday 06 May 2010 12:32:13 Ian Johnson wrote:
> Hmm...a relevant question:
> .i ko'a goi lo fasnu .i ko'e goi lo fasnu
>
> Does {ko'a du ko'e} have a defined truth value now? If so, what is it? (I
> suspect that it doesn't have a truth value yet.)

It doesn't. "lo fasnu" can refer to any event, or to events in general, and 
there's no way to tell from those two sentences whether the two occurrences 
of "lo fasnu" refer to the same event.

